+# Threshold Feature Implementation Summary
+
+## Overview
+Added threshold gating to `frai eval` command and `frai-core` SDK to enable CI pipelines to fail when evaluation metrics fall below configured minimums.
+
+## Files Modified
+
+### frai-core (SDK)
+
+#### `packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`
+- Updated `generateReport()` function signature to accept optional `thresholds` parameter
+- Added threshold validation logic that:
+  - Compares each metric's score against its minimum threshold
+  - Treats missing scores (null) as failures
+  - Sets `report.passed = true` only if all thresholds pass
+  - Adds `report.thresholds` array with one entry per threshold containing `{ metric, min, score, passed }`
+- Added JSDoc documentation for the function
+
+#### `packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`
+- Updated `toMarkdown()` to include "Thresholds" section when thresholds are present
+- Each threshold shows: metric name, PASS/FAIL status, minimum value, and actual score
+
+#### `packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js`
+- Added 4 new test cases:
+  1. `generates report with passing thresholds` - verifies all thresholds pass
+  2. `generates report with failing thresholds` - verifies failure detection
+  3. `handles missing metric score in thresholds` - verifies null scores fail
+  4. (Existing test) `generates and writes report` - still works without thresholds
+
+#### `packages/frai-core/README.md`
+- Updated CLI reference for `frai eval` command to document `--threshold` option
+- Added SDK usage example showing how to use thresholds with `generateReport()`
+
+### frai-cli (CLI)
+
+#### `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`
+- Updated `EvalOptions` interface to include `threshold?: string[]`
+- Added `parseThreshold()` function to:
+  - Validate threshold format: `<metric>=<number>`
+  - Validate min value is between 0 and 1
+  - Return parsed `{ metric, min }` or null if invalid
+- Updated `runEvalCommand()` to:
+  - Parse and validate all thresholds before evaluation
+  - Exit with code 2 if any threshold is malformed or unknown
+  - List valid metric IDs when threshold references unknown metric
+  - Pass thresholds object to `generateReport()`
+  - Exit with code 1 if any threshold fails (after writing report)
+  - Exit with code 0 otherwise (implicit)
+- Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option with accumulation callback to support multiple uses
+- Option is optional; without it, behavior is unchanged
+
+#### `packages/frai-cli/README.md`
+- Updated `frai eval` command documentation to include `--threshold` option details
+- Documented exit codes: 0 for pass/no thresholds, 1 for failure, 2 for usage error
+- Listed valid metric IDs
+
+## Feature Behavior
+
+### CLI Usage
+```bash
+# Single threshold
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9
+
+# Multiple thresholds
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95
+
+# Without thresholds (original behavior)
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json
+```
+
+### Exit Codes
+- `0` - All thresholds passed (or no thresholds provided)
+- `1` - One or more thresholds failed
+- `2` - Malformed threshold or unknown metric (no report written)
+
+### Report Output
+- **JSON**: Adds `passed` boolean and `thresholds` array at top level (when thresholds used)
+- **Markdown**: Adds "Thresholds" section with PASS/FAIL status for each metric
+
+### Error Handling
+- Malformed threshold format: `"Invalid threshold format. Use: --threshold <metric>=<number>"`
+- Invalid min value (not 0-1): Caught by format validation
+- Unknown metric: `"Unknown metric id."` with list of valid metric IDs
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+- Fully backward compatible - existing scripts without `--threshold` work unchanged
+- `generateReport()` works with or without thresholds
+- Report format is extended but not broken for existing users
